## Tasks

### Task 1 — Email ingest skill

Path: `Pathfinder/lib/ingest/skills/ingest-email.ts`

Logic:
1. Daily cron (08:00 PT) scans designated email accounts (kyle@, keenan@, curtis@, team@unicron.systems) via Gmail MCP
2. Filter: emails received in last 24 hours, not yet ingested (track in `nervous_system.ingest_processed` table or use a `processed_at` field)
3. For each: extract decisions, action items, insights using same structured-output prompt as call ingest, adjusted for email context
4. Skip mass/promotional email (heuristic: from-domain blacklist, unsubscribe headers, etc.)
5. Return one of `records | NO_SIGNAL | ABSTAIN`

Per-customer attribution: if email mentions a customer by name in body or subject, attach `customer_id` to ledger row.

### Task 2 — Multi-fork sprint contract

Path: `Pathfinder/lib/sprint-fork.ts` (and Cowork skill at `Cowork/skills/multi-fork-sprint.md` per skill plugin convention)

Contract:
- Sprint declares scoring function before launch (judge agent identifier OR hard metric)
- N parallel Claude Code prompts dispatched (default N=3) via `Task` tool
- Each runs in its own worktree (using-git-worktrees skill)
- Each produces a candidate diff and self-evaluation
- Scoring agent ranks candidates
- Pruning rule: keep top K (default K=1), archive losers with reasons in `vault/Memory/sprint_forks/<sprint_id>/`
- Reinforcement: winning approach's pattern logged as a `signal` of type `PATTERN`

Expose as a Cowork skill so future Cowork chats can request multi-fork sprints with one invocation.

### Task 3 — Bounded peer attention configuration

Configure Cowork peer subscriptions per SPEC section 16:
- Each Cowork chat declares peer watches in its session-start memory load
- Persistent agents declare in `agents.config.watches_*`
- Implement Supabase Realtime channel with topic filtering for agent peer attention
- Each Cowork chat reads peer's last `vault/Memory/cowork/<chat_name>/latest.md` at session start

Document the subscription rules table in `vault/Memory/wiki/how-it-works.md` (stub for Sprint 6).

### Task 4 — Sprint runs tracking table

Add `nervous_system.sprint_runs` table for Atrium Sprints view in Work tab:

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS nervous_system.sprint_runs (
  id uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  sprint_name text not null,
  sprint_prompt_path text,
  surface text,
  status text default 'in_process' check (status in ('in_process','deployed','review','bug_fixes','verified','halted')),
  started_at timestamptz default now(),
  completed_at timestamptz,
  evidence_link text,
  kanban_card_id text,
  fork_count integer default 1,
  fork_winner_id uuid,
  log_tail jsonb default '[]'::jsonb,
  created_by jsonb,
  ttl_days integer default 90,
  last_touched timestamptz default now()
);
```

Update Conductor and per-sprint prompts to write/update this table at sprint start and end (retroactive entries for Sprints 0-4 acceptable).

### Task 5 — Atrium People tab

Path: `unicron-platform/src/atrium/People.tsx` and sub-components

**5.1 Customers pipeline** (`CustomersPipeline.tsx`)
- Drag-drop kanban view of `nervous_system.customers` rows by status
- Stages: Cold, Discovery, Proposal, Contract, Onboarding, Active, Churned
- Per-customer card: name, primary contact, last contact date, next action item
- Drag updates `customers.status`; audit logged

**5.2 Per-customer health card** (drill-in from pipeline)
- Usage frequency (active tenants only; pulled from product analytics — Pathfinder for Zedcor)
- Engagement depth (counts of Slack threads, calls, emails about this customer in last 30 days)
- Last contact date and channel
- Contract milestones
- Sentiment signal (Analyst-derived from ledger sentiment scores)
- Recent activity feed (filtered ledger by `customer_id`)
- Action items related (filtered action_items by `customer_id`)

**5.3 Team my-day views** (`TeamMyDay.tsx`)
- List of team_members with avatars, roles
- Click into member: their open DRIs, calendar today, last digest read state, pending Verified reviews, action items requested-by and requested-of
- Capacity heatmap: visual indicator weighted by priority and due date

**5.4 Network** (`Network.tsx`)
- Advisors, warm contacts, contributors as a list (data sourced from `vault/Memory/people/<name>.md` if present, plus a future `nervous_system.contacts` table — start lightweight with vault-only)
- Last-touch dates per contact (from ledger `participants` unless explicit `nervous_system.contacts` table is added)
- "Who introduced who" lightweight graph

**5.5 Hiring** (`Hiring.tsx`)
- Pipeline (Sourced, Screening, Interview, Offer, Accepted, Declined)
- Hidden when no active candidates (gated by env or empty data)

### Task 6 — Atrium Money tab

Path: `unicron-platform/src/atrium/Money.tsx` and sub-components

**6.1 Accounts** (`Accounts.tsx`)
- Read from `nervous_system.connected_services` table (add this table as part of Sprint 5):
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS nervous_system.connected_services (
  id uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  name text not null,
  category text,
  status text default 'unknown' check (status in ('healthy','degraded','broken','unknown')),
  monthly_cost_usd numeric,
  last_billed_at date,
  last_health_check_at timestamptz,
  owner_team_member_id uuid references nervous_system.team_members(id),
  config_url text,
  notes text
);
```
- Render as a list with status, cost, owner, link to provider
- Auto-detect status via Sprint 3 services-health logic (extends here)
- Replace Notion accounts page (link to migrate manually)

**6.2 Runway** (`Runway.tsx`)
- Cash on hand (manual entry initially; link to bank when connector exists)
- Monthly burn (sum of `connected_services.monthly_cost_usd` + manually entered payroll)
- Runway months (cash / burn)
- Burn-down chart (Recharts)

**6.3 Revenue** (`Revenue.tsx`)
- MRR/ARR if Stripe connected; otherwise show "no revenue connector configured"
- Per-customer revenue (when connector exists)
- Pipeline-weighted forecast (customers in Proposal/Contract stages × probability)

**6.4 Expenses** (`Expenses.tsx`)
- Categorized monthly view: infrastructure, services, payroll, contractors, marketing, other
- Auto-imported from `connected_services` where automatic; manual entry forms otherwise
- "Manual" badge on hand-entered fields

**6.5 Cost spike alerts** (`CostSpikes.tsx`)
- Analyst flags abnormal spend per category (>2x rolling 30-day average)
- Render as list with timestamp, category, baseline, spike value
- Click for detail and acknowledge

